Author: saadahmed95 <saad.ahmed95@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 2 11:51:27 2026 +0200

    feat(ws): abandon a turn when its socket closes

    Closing a socket stopped nothing: the turn kept generating billed
    tokens, kept calling tools for a user who had left and kept writing
    to a socket nobody read. Each connection now has one AbortController,
    aborted first in its close listener, before the session teardown and
    onDisconnect, and passed to handleMessage. The handler drops a turn
    whose signal is already aborted, hands the signal to the run, stops
    pulling chunks once it aborts and sends no stream_end. The
    orchestrator forwards the signal to the provider as params.signal,
    composes it into each ToolContext.signal, ends a tool round at once
    when it aborts, records nothing that round produced, and treats a
    failure after the abort as a controlled stop: no onError, no
    afterModelResponse, afterSession once. A missed heartbeat and stop()
    reach the same path.

    Coverage floors raised to the new measurement, identical over two
    runs: orchestration 291/301 st, 159/173 br, 76/78 fn, 246/254 ln
    (was 273/283, 143/157, 75/77, 234/242); global 734/805 st, 380/456
    br, 176/196 fn, 648/706 ln (was 724/796, 374/451, 175/195, 639/698).

    Fixes #49

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

